# CampusConnect behind Caddy - HTTPS without any application code.
#
# The C++ server keeps speaking HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8080. Caddy terminates TLS in
# front of it. That is the standard production arrangement: the app does not need
# to know about certificates, renewals, or HTTPS internals.
#
# LOCAL DEMO (no domain, no cost):
#   brew install caddy
#   sudo caddy trust     # one-time: installs Caddy's local CA in the trust store
#   caddy run            # uses this file, listening on https://localhost
#   # start the app with:
#   CC_COOKIE_SECURE=1 CC_HSTS=1 CC_BASE_URL=https://localhost make run
#
# PRODUCTION (a real domain pointed at the machine, ports 80/443 reachable):
#   comment out the localhost block and uncomment the domain block below.
#   Caddy obtains and renews a free Let's Encrypt certificate automatically.
#   Then run the app with CC_COOKIE_SECURE=1 CC_HSTS=1 CC_BASE_URL=https://your.domain

localhost {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}

